@startuml component-architecture
!theme plain
top to bottom direction
title Staged plugin split (ADR-0034)

package "Stage A — one plugin, dev10x (no user-visible change)" {
  package "src/dev10x (one PyPI package)" {
    [dev10x.core] as CORE
    [dev10x.qa] as QA
    [dev10x.infra] as INFRA
    [dev10x.db] as DB
    [dev10x.comm] as COMM
    [dev10x.skillmgmt] as SKILLMGMT
    [dev10x.tasks] as TASKS
    [dev10x.scoping] as SCOPING
    [dev10x.coding] as CODING
  }
  [cli MCP server\nregister() per namespace\nmcp~__plugin_dev10x_cli~__*] as CLI
  [hooks + config fragments\nkeyed by future plugin] as FRAG
  [dev10x skill rename\n+ user-config migration] as RENAME
}

QA --> CORE
INFRA --> CORE
DB --> CORE
COMM --> CORE
SKILLMGMT --> CORE
TASKS --> CORE
SCOPING --> CORE
CODING --> CORE
CLI --> CORE
FRAG --> CORE
RENAME --> CORE

package "Stage B — extraction, one plugin at a time" {
  [dev10x (core)\nkeeps name, MCP servers, hooks] as KEEP
  [B1 QA] as P1
  [B2 infrastructure] as P2
  [B3 databases] as P3
  [B4 communication] as P4
  [B5 skill management] as P5
  [B6 task management] as P6
  [B7 tickets + scoping] as P7
  [B9 coding] as P9
}

P1 ..> KEEP
P2 ..> KEEP
P3 ..> KEEP
P4 ..> KEEP
P5 ..> KEEP
P6 ..> KEEP
P7 ..> KEEP
P9 ..> KEEP

note bottom of KEEP
  B8: core is finalized in place (what remains
  under the dev10x name). Each move runs the
  rename tool for its own skills only.
end note
@enduml
